							<div class="quoteheader"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=320.msg16821#msg16821">Quote from: A Mammal on May 03, 2005, 05:23:11 pm</a></div><div class="quote">I have nothing against anyone really, but its kinda funny how you claim they have reading problems. They get the same message from the same post. Two people mis-reading the same thing might not be the reader, but maybe the writer?<br /></div><br />Maybe then you can show me where I said that his suggestion was not valid? Quite the opposite, it&#039;s a fine suggestion, I just didn&#039;t care much for the packaging. Maybe they have a right to post their elitist and condescending opinions here on this message board, but then I&#039;ve just as much right to call them asses for it.<br /><br />I&#039;m simply tired of seeing so many posts from bitter or jaded or petty people taking time to come to a message board for a game they no longer play or for a server they&#039;re no longer on just to make sure that no one forgets how cool they are and to make sure that they think their accomplishments don&#039;t mean jack. Frankly, I don&#039;t care what anyone thinks about me or my guild, but the constant air of nastiness gets rather old. ...and not to single Matteo&#039;s post out, it just happened to be the one I finally felt the need to respond to.<br /><br />Justyse gives a great list of examples of exactly what I mean back on page 187. Those happen to be all Toastie quotes, but he&#039;s not the only one.<br /><br /><div class="quoteheader"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=320.msg16820#msg16820">Quote from: matteo on May 03, 2005, 05:19:46 pm</a></div><div class="quote">I still play EQ on occasion.&nbsp; It is a fun game.&nbsp; If you don&#039;t care about my opinions then dont read them.&nbsp; I really couldn&#039;t care less.&nbsp; It will be a cold day in hell before some prepubescent dumb fuck like you decides where I can and cannot post.&nbsp; If my posts bother you so much go get some counceling.<br /></div><br />You imply that we&#039;re all idiots and don&#039;t expect for someone to reply to you about that? And good job backpedaling about the slant your putting on the encounter. First it&#039;s stupid to be fighting over an encounter 4 expansions old, now it&#039;s a very good accomplishment for a guild at that level. If it&#039;s such a great accomplishment (now) then maybe you can understand why we might want to do it on our own? I think having good relations with other guilds is great, but that doesn&#039;t mean we should have to buddy up to beat mobs. And yeah, we beat him once, but it&#039;s still a challenging encounter.<br /><br />lol, prepubescent dumb fuck...gold.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
